WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.159 --> 00:00:16.081
breath came in ragged gasps as he ran through the darkness.

2
00:00:17.302 --> 00:00:19.984
He could feel powerful magic swirling around him.

3
00:00:21.165 --> 00:00:24.327
He did his best to avoid the magic energy, but it wasn't easy.

4
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:28.470
It was so dark he could barely see his hand in front of his face.

5
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:30.412
Where was he?

6
00:00:30.976 --> 00:00:33.477
What sort of place could be so dark and frightening?

7
00:00:34.598 --> 00:00:36.098
Could it be the Cave of the Unknown?

8
00:00:36.718 --> 00:00:39.079
Was he deep within its endless, winding tunnels?

9
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.581
He touched his shoulder, but there was no crawler there to lead him out.

10
00:00:44.462 --> 00:00:47.663
He could be lost forever "No!"

11
00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:49.584
he shouted as panic overtook him.

12
00:00:50.624 --> 00:00:54.326
He stumbled and almost fell, but he caught himself and kept running.

13
00:00:54.786 --> 00:00:55.886
He couldn't stop running.

14
00:00:56.807 --> 00:01:01.464
He had to find to find "Zann?"

15
00:01:01.965 --> 00:01:02.665
a voice called.

16
00:01:03.266 --> 00:01:04.827
It sounded distant and faint.

17
00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:07.309
Zann's heart jumped with hope.

18
00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:08.730
He knew that voice!

19
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.232
"Dad?" he shouted.

20
00:01:11.252 --> 00:01:12.332
"Where are you?

21
00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:16.255
Dad!" Zann leaped forward to follow the voice.

22
00:01:16.636 --> 00:01:18.497
But someone grabbed his shoulder from behind.

23
00:01:19.438 --> 00:01:22.520
Zann felt the person's sharp, strong fingers tightening.

24
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.281
Or were they claws?

25
00:01:25.422 --> 00:01:27.924
"Ow!" he cried, struggling to free himself.

26
00:01:30.752 --> 00:01:31.012
"Let me go!

27
00:01:31.032 --> 00:01:32.974
I have to save my parents—they're in danger!"

28
00:01:33.954 --> 00:01:35.655
But the hand only gripped more tightly.

29
00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:40.399
"Zann!" the voice came again, sounding even fainter.

30
00:01:40.419 --> 00:01:42.380
"Zann!" "Zann?"

31
00:01:43.101 --> 00:01:46.503
Zann opened his eyes and saw his grandfather peering down at him.

32
00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:51.006
"Boz?" he mumbled, squinting in the bright morning light.

33
00:01:52.147 --> 00:01:53.648
Boz let go of Zann's shoulder.

34
00:01:53.668 --> 00:01:54.889
"Are you okay?

35
00:01:55.529 --> 00:01:57.030
You were shouting in your sleep."

36
00:01:58.071 --> 00:01:59.472
Zann sat up and looked around.

37
00:02:00.948 --> 00:02:02.989
He was in his familiar bedroom in Swamp Bottom.

38
00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:05.149
Well, mostly familiar.

39
00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:10.311
Boz had rebuilt the house as soon as they'd returned from the capital the previous day.

40
00:02:11.511 --> 00:02:14.172
It looked almost the same as it had before Morb destroyed it.

41
00:02:15.072 --> 00:02:16.532
But a few things were different now.

42
00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:18.893
The kitchen was a little bigger.

43
00:02:19.893 --> 00:02:22.234
Some of the furniture was a new color or shape.

44
00:02:23.314 --> 00:02:26.255
The hole that Zing had once blasted in Zann's window was gone.

45
00:02:26.275 --> 00:02:29.876
"Zann?" Boz sounded concerned.

46
00:02:30.432 --> 00:02:31.972
"Did you have a nightmare?"

47
00:02:31.992 --> 00:02:34.613
"Yes," Zann mumbled.

48
00:02:35.193 --> 00:02:36.974
"I mean no, not really.

49
00:02:37.814 --> 00:02:38.274
Sort of."

50
00:02:39.134 --> 00:02:41.355
Boz sighed, rubbing his long nose.

51
00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:46.596
"I'm afraid it was a mistake to take you to the Cave of the Unknown.

52
00:02:47.537 --> 00:02:49.037
Obviously it affected you.

53
00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:50.257
I'm sorry."

54
00:02:50.277 --> 00:02:52.218
"I'm not sorry."

55
00:02:52.618 --> 00:02:55.099
Zann shrugged and swung his legs over the edge of the bed.

56
00:02:55.119 --> 00:02:56.699
"I'm glad I went."

57
00:02:57.839 --> 00:02:59.540
He shot a look at the bedside table.

58
00:03:00.468 --> 00:03:04.549
The message stone was there, tucked behind a framed blink image of his parents.

59
00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.950
Boz didn't notice the look.

60
00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.670
He seemed distracted.

61
00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:12.511
"I'll go and conjure some breakfast," he said.

62
00:03:12.531 --> 00:03:14.052
"Hurry and get dressed."

63
00:03:15.332 --> 00:03:17.633
As Boz left the room, Zing scurried in.

64
00:03:17.653 --> 00:03:20.874
"Morning, little buddy," Zann said.

65
00:03:21.894 --> 00:03:23.534
He stood up and glanced out the window.

66
00:03:24.475 --> 00:03:28.536
The grass had a purplish sheen, indicating that it had rained overnight.

67
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.201
But the sun was bright and the aurora birds were singing.

68
00:03:33.221 --> 00:03:35.022
"Nice day.

69
00:03:35.742 --> 00:03:39.544
Too bad I have to spend it here in Swamp Bottom," Zann muttered.

70
00:03:40.364 --> 00:03:42.445
For a moment his dream came back to him.

71
00:03:43.265 --> 00:03:46.827
It reminded him of the dream he'd had outside the Cave of the Unknown.

72
00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:51.929
This latest dream had been scary and confusing, just like the previous one.

73
00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:55.851
But he'd felt so close to reaching his parents this time!

74
00:03:57.511 --> 00:03:58.632
Those were just dreams though.

75
00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.582
How was he ever going to find his parents for real?

76
00:04:01.602 --> 00:04:06.567
"It's hopeless as long as I'm stuck here," he told Zing.

77
00:04:06.587 --> 00:04:10.310
"I need to figure out how to get to one of those wormholes."

78
00:04:11.311 --> 00:04:14.734
Zann rubbed his hands together and pictured his favorite outfit.

79
00:04:15.674 --> 00:04:19.318
A second later his pajamas disappeared, and he was fully dressed.

80
00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:23.221
He stepped over to his dresser and picked up a comb.

81
00:04:23.241 --> 00:04:26.364
"I have to come up with a plan," he said.

82
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.884
"I could probably make it to First City in five or six zaps if I really tried.

83
00:04:32.825 --> 00:04:37.729
Once I got there, I could rest for a while and then hop through that Wormwood wormhole."

84
00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:42.213
Zing responded by shooting a small flame at Zann's leg.

85
00:04:43.174 --> 00:04:45.356
Zann glanced at the dragon and sighed.

86
00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:49.499
"I know it's a crazy plan," he admitted.

87
00:04:49.519 --> 00:04:54.964
"But school starts again in a few days, and then I won't have time to do anything!"

88
00:04:55.808 --> 00:04:59.550
He seemed no closer to finding his parents than he'd been before his adventures.

89
00:05:00.371 --> 00:05:03.012
It was almost as if none of them had ever happened.

90
00:05:03.752 --> 00:05:06.994
When Zann reached the breakfast table, his grandfather was waiting for him.

91
00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:13.197
"Sit down, boy," Boz said, nodding toward a bowl of rice with glowberry sauce.

92
00:05:13.217 --> 00:05:15.398
"I want to talk to you about something."

93
00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.220
Zann sat down and grabbed his food.

94
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.701
"Um, okay," he said.

95
00:05:20.721 --> 00:05:27.304
"Recent events have made me think about a few things," Boz said, rubbing his nose and staring at

96
00:05:27.364 --> 00:05:28.185
Zann solemnly.

97
00:05:28.205 --> 00:05:31.085
"You're growing up so fast, Zann.

98
00:05:31.886 --> 00:05:34.866
You remind me of your mother when she was your age.

99
00:05:35.527 --> 00:05:41.488
She always wanted excitement and adventure too Zann kept his eyes on his food.

100
00:05:42.568 --> 00:05:45.669
His grandfather often lectured him about being too adventurous.

101
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:51.091
But no matter what Boz said, Zann was never going to give up on finding his parents.

102
00:05:51.111 --> 00:05:56.629
"I have to remember that you're not a child anymore," Boz went on.

103
00:05:57.049 --> 00:06:01.032
"It might be time to—" Just then a message moth flapped in.

104
00:06:01.613 --> 00:06:02.994
It landed on Zann's arm.

105
00:06:03.014 --> 00:06:07.578
"It's from Perda," said Zann, scanning the insect's wings.

106
00:06:07.598 --> 00:06:11.141
"She wants me to meet her in the swamp right away."

107
00:06:11.821 --> 00:06:14.203
He gulped down the last bite of rice and stood up.

108
00:06:14.223 --> 00:06:16.886
"Wait a minute, Zann," Boz said.

109
00:06:16.906 --> 00:06:19.248
"I really think we need to talk."

110
00:06:19.268 --> 00:06:21.089
"Can it wait until later?"

111
00:06:21.329 --> 00:06:21.890
Zann said.

112
00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.032
"I should find out what Perda wants."

113
00:06:24.997 --> 00:06:29.143
As Boz sighed and nodded, Zann grabbed Zing and zapped out of the house.
